<h2>What Is Claude Code</h2>
<p>Think of Claude Code as <strong>an AI agent that runs in your local environment (your own PC)</strong>. Unlike web chat, it reads and edits the files on your computer directly and runs commands to get work done. You work by <strong>creating one folder per project and staying inside that folder</strong>. On Windows you normally run it from the <strong>PowerShell</strong> terminal.</p>

<h3>How it differs from existing services</h3>
<div class="tbl-wrap">
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr><th>Form</th><th>Characteristics</th><th>Freedom</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>Web browser (Claude &middot; ChatGPT &middot; Gemini)</td><td>Using AI inside the browser's constrained environment. You have to upload files one by one</td><td>Most limited</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Claude desktop app</td><td>Runs locally, but has constraints compared to the terminal</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Claude Code (terminal)</strong></td><td>Direct access to the files in the folder you launched it from. Work as freely as you like</td><td>Most free</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
<p>Get just a little comfortable with the terminal environment and you can use it far more freely, much as you would use ordinary AI chat.</p>

